{"name":"Queencore","title":"Queencore","revision":230383,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Queencore","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Queencore is a more mature, regal variant of Princesscore and a subgenre of Royalcore. Queencore, as a whole, draws from matriarchal and regal roles in many monarchies. One example of such would be the former Queen of England, Elizabeth II, and Princess Diana, of England and Wales both. As being the head of a monarchy, a queen would have to lead one's country through hardships such as famine and wars. This guidance leads to an air of regalia as they handle these issues with grace and care for their peoples."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visual"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Most visuals can be taken from castle exteriors, interiors, and grounds. This can include throne rooms, royal chambers, and gardens. Examples include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Thrones"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crowns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Capes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ornate staircases"},{"kind":"list","text":"Personal libraries"},{"kind":"list","text":"Scepters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jewelry"},{"kind":"list","text":"Intricate gardens"},{"kind":"list","text":"Roses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Horses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marble"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swords and daggers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Veils"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ballgowns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dark wood"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tall ceilings"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fashion may be taken directly from historical accounts or may be modernized. Real life examples can include historical figures like Queen Victoria for a more historical approach, or figures like Kate Middleton and Meghan Markle for more modern fashion. Fictional examples can include Queen Calanthe from The Witcher, Cersei Lannister from Game of Thrones, Mary, Queen of Scots from Reign, and The Countess from American Horror Story (for a more creative twist). Staples include intricate embroidery, beading, jewel and metal embellishments, darker or richer colors, and long sleeves. Suggestions include:"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Clothing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Floor-length formalwear Ballgowns Wide-legged jumpsuits or pants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Modest-length day dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fitted slacks / jeans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tailored blouses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fitted suits in royal colors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long jackets and coats / cloaks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corsets / shifts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long dressing robes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Damasc, jacquard and brocade"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heeled footwear"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Accessories"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crown or tiara"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lace gloves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Victorian-style lace collars"},{"kind":"list","text":"Velvet or lace headbands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chokers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vintage brooches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Statement rings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Embellished hair clips"},{"kind":"list","text":"Elaborate earrings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tulle or lace parasol"},{"kind":"list","text":"Precious metals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jewels"},{"kind":"list","text":"Clutch bags"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Makeup"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"As queencore is associated with regality and grace, one would be able to create such a look with the following:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Light foundation"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bold eyeshadow"},{"kind":"list","text":"Red or pink lipstick"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Playlists"},{"kind":"list","text":"royalcore aesthetic playlist (spotify) by miraya ☁️"},{"kind":"list","text":"dark royalty core aesthetic playlist"},{"kind":"list","text":"a playlist for waltzing with your enemy (dark royalty core)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Royalcore Playlist Nr. 1"},{"kind":"list","text":"dark academia x royal core playlist"},{"kind":"list","text":"you've just killed the king and now you're the reigning monarch"},{"kind":"list","text":"crying on your throne in regret"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Historic Examples"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mary, Queen of Scots 1542 - 1587"},{"kind":"list","text":"Queen Elizabeth II 1926 - 2022"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maria Theresa of Austria 1717 - 1780"},{"kind":"list","text":"Catherine the Great of Russia 1729 - 1796"},{"kind":"list","text":"Anne Boleyn of England 1501 - 1536"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nefertiti of Egypt 1370 - 1330 BC"},{"kind":"list","text":"Victoria of England 1819 - 1901"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marie-Antoinette of France 1755 - 1793"},{"kind":"list","text":"Elizabeth I of England 1533 - 1603"},{"kind":"list","text":"Catherine of Aragon 1485 - 1536"},{"kind":"list","text":"Eleanor of Aquitaine 1122 - 1204"},{"kind":"list","text":"Empress Theodora 500 - 548"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hatshepsut of Egypt 1508 - 1458 BC"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wu Zetian 624 - 705"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cleopatra VII, Ptolemaic Queen of Egypt 69 - 30 BC"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mary I of England 1516 - 1558"},{"kind":"list","text":"Elizabeth \"Sissi\" of Austria 1837 - 1898"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"For a more complete list, see List of queens regnant and Lists of queens."}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c0/CvygNIXWEAYgRaa.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20201019162835","caption":"CvygNIXWEAYgRaa","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:CvygNIXWEAYgRaa.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0825-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/91/Crown.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20201019162624","caption":"Queencore · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Crown.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0825-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}